      "role": "user",
      "content": "That's a good start, the tone is definitely there. I like the \"presence of something that waits\" bit.\n\nThe thing is, when I ran this through the automated validator, the depth score came back way lower than what the engine usually requires for a main questline. It's only about 65 words. I get that I told you not to pad it, but if it's too short, the quest system won't even register it as a \"substantial\" encounter. \n\nCan you expand on this? Try to weave in more of that lore about the old gods or the \"unraveling\" you mentioned. Just please, keep it meaningful—don't just repeat the same ideas or use filler words, I need actual world-building that adds weight to the dialogue.",
      "source": "evaluator"
    },
